<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  QBX-246: verify-undo reads EVERY root, not the master alone.
  QBX-249: and an arrangement-side add-track's inverse now lands in its own
  root, which is what lets this case carry the fixture QBX-246 had to drop.

  WHAT verify-undo USED TO DO. It captured the master's track count, undid
  everything, asserted the master was empty, redid, and asserted the master's
  count had come back. A case that built tracks inside an arrangement and
  undid them badly passed that: the master's count had not moved, and nothing
  else was looked at. It now snapshots a count PER ROOT and compares the whole
  map, so a root that fails to come back is a missing key rather than a count
  nobody compares.

  WHAT THIS CASE GATES, in two halves:

    THE ROOT SET. `Drums` is created inside the undo range, so after a full
    undo it must be GONE (create-arrangement's inverse unregisters it) and
    after the matching redo it must be BACK.

    THE COUNTS, which is QBX-249's half. The arrangement gets TWO lanes and
    the master ONE, deliberately unequal: a mis-rooted inverse removes from
    the wrong root, and with equal counts the arithmetic still adds up.

  THE BITING ARM is the undo. Measured on a main baseline (d14d5522) before
  the fix, with this fixture:

      verify-undo: after undo, root Drums has 2 track(s), expected 0
                   (every root: <master>=0,Drums=2)

  one undo of an arrangement-side add-track removed a lane from the MASTER and
  left the arrangement's standing. The knock-on is why it stayed silent:
  SRemoveArrangementAction refuses to drop a root that still holds lanes, with
  good reason (its inverse rebuilds an EMPTY mixer), so the rest of the undo
  then refused too and the project was left with the master emptied and the
  arrangement intact. Nothing reported an error.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="arrangement_undo_checks_every_root">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <set-track-name trackPath="0" name="MasterLane"/>

    <!-- Created INSIDE the undo range: its unregistration is part of what is
         under test, as are the two lanes put in it. -->
    <create-arrangement name="Drums"/>
    <add-track arrangement="Drums" index="-1"/>
    <add-track arrangement="Drums" index="-1"/>

    <assert-track-count arrangement="" count="1"/>
    <assert-track-count arrangement="Drums" count="2"/>
  </actions>

  <verify-undo/>

</SActionScript>
